# MZO Reports: follow the repo rules

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) before any change, then the guide for the area you touch in `docs/` (index in [README.md](../../README.md#documentation)).

## Must follow

- Local dev writes to **production** (Supabase, Google Sheets, Apps Script). Never save, upload, sync, allot, cancel, approve or delete while testing.
- Login office scope is `mzo_scope.js` (`window.MzoScope`) only: `MzoScope.filterRows` right after parsing. No per-page office preferences.
- Load report data through `mzo_data_hub.js` (`UI.load` / `waitForDataset` / `get`). Do not fetch a Google Sheet from a page when a `DATASETS` key exists, and never proxy report data through Vercel.
- New and rebuilt pages use the UI kit (`mzo_theme.css`, `mzo_ui.js`) and the structure in `docs/design-system.md`.
- Bump `CACHE_NAME` in `sw.js` and `version.json` when users must receive changed files; add new pages to `isNetworkFirstPath`; new folders need a `vercel.json` static build entry.
- Do not rename or move served pages (bookmarked URLs).
- Production is only https://mzo-reports.vercel.app; deploy rules in `docs/deploy.md`.

## Keep the docs current

If you add a page, dataset, API, env var, auth flag, scope rule or a pattern others should copy, update the matching file in `docs/` (and `AGENTS.md` for repo-wide rules) in the same change.
